From: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] isvp-t41: write the default environment to flash on first boot

A board flashed for the first time has a blank environment sector. U-Boot copes
on its own - it falls back to the environment compiled into it - but that
fallback lives only in RAM, and Linux does not read it. fw_printenv goes to the
MTD device, finds a bad CRC there, and quietly answers from its own
three-variable default:

    Warning: Bad CRC, using default environment
    bootcmd=bootp; setenv bootargs root=/dev/nfs ...
    bootdelay=5
    baudrate=115200

So every lookup the startup scripts make - soc, sensor, osmem, totalmem - comes
back empty, and the camera boots but comes up without video. Nothing in the log
points at the environment, because from userspace's point of view there simply
is one.

Writing the defaults out the first time they are used fixes it at the source:
one copy of the truth, in the .env file, reaching both U-Boot and Linux. It also
repairs a sector whose contents have been corrupted. Afterwards the environment
loads from flash, GD_FLG_ENV_DEFAULT is clear, and this is a no-op.

board_late_init() is made unconditional and the pad-init call moved inside it,
so the two features no longer depend on each other being enabled.

Signed-off-by: Oskari Rauta <oskari.rauta@gmail.com>
---
--- a/board/ingenic/isvp-t41/isvp-t41.c
+++ b/board/ingenic/isvp-t41/isvp-t41.c
@@ -9,6 +9,7 @@
  */
 
 #include <dm.h>
+#include <env.h>
 #include <init.h>
 #include <ram.h>
 #include <stdio.h>
@@ -217,20 +218,42 @@
 	return 0;
 }
 
-#ifdef CONFIG_T41_VENDOR_PAD_INIT
-/*
- * Re-apply the vendor CPM state after all of U-Boot proper's own
- * driver probing: the DM clk/mmc path re-dirties MSC0CDR (stale
- * CE + divider) after board_init(), and Linux inherits whatever is
- * left here. board_late_init() is the last hook before autoboot;
- * the boot command itself (sf read + bootm) touches no clocks.
- */
 int board_late_init(void)
 {
+#ifdef CONFIG_T41_VENDOR_PAD_INIT
+	/*
+	 * Re-apply the vendor CPM state after all of U-Boot proper's own
+	 * driver probing: the DM clk/mmc path re-dirties MSC0CDR (stale
+	 * CE + divider) after board_init(), and Linux inherits whatever is
+	 * left here. This is the last hook before autoboot; the boot
+	 * command itself (sf read + bootm) touches no clocks.
+	 */
 	t41_vendor_cpm_state();
+#endif
+
+#ifdef CONFIG_T41_SAVE_DEFAULT_ENV
+	/*
+	 * A board flashed for the first time has a blank environment sector.
+	 * U-Boot copes on its own - it falls back to the environment compiled
+	 * into this binary - but that fallback lives only in RAM, while Linux
+	 * reads the environment straight off the MTD device. fw_printenv finds
+	 * a bad CRC there and quietly answers from its own three-variable
+	 * default instead, so the startup scripts get nothing for soc, sensor
+	 * or totalmem and the camera comes up without video, with no error that
+	 * points at the cause.
+	 *
+	 * So write the defaults out the first time they are used. Afterwards
+	 * the environment loads from flash, the flag is clear and this is a
+	 * no-op. It also repairs a sector that has been corrupted.
+	 */
+	if (gd->flags & GD_FLG_ENV_DEFAULT) {
+		printf("Env:   none in flash, saving the built-in default\n");
+		env_save();
+	}
+#endif
+
 	return 0;
 }
-#endif
 
 int checkboard(void)
 {
--- a/arch/mips/mach-xburst/t41/Kconfig
+++ b/arch/mips/mach-xburst/t41/Kconfig
@@ -42,4 +42,19 @@
 	  initialise. Harmless but board-specific; leave disabled for
 	  other T41 boards.
 
+config T41_SAVE_DEFAULT_ENV
+	bool "Write the built-in default environment to flash on first boot"
+	select BOARD_LATE_INIT
+	default y
+	help
+	  When the environment sector is blank or its CRC is bad, U-Boot
+	  falls back to the environment compiled into it - but only in
+	  RAM. Linux reads the environment from the MTD device instead,
+	  so on a freshly flashed board it sees nothing, and userspace
+	  that looks up soc or sensor there comes up misconfigured.
+
+	  With this enabled the defaults are written out once, the first
+	  time they are used, which also repairs a corrupted sector. Say
+	  n only if the board must never write its own environment.
+
 endif
